I've revised the description to match what has been built and what the schema review of 2026-10-08 agreed (see the *Revision* panel at the top). The main changes:

* *The PPDB's {{SSSource}} is renamed {{SSObservation}}.* Its structure and meaning now differ from the alert's {{SSSource}}: in an alert, {{SSSource}} says that a known object is nearby; in the PPDB, each row is one MPC-accepted observation of the object, keyed by the MPC's {{obsid}}. Renaming the alert's version would break compatibility, so the PPDB table is renamed instead. The alert's {{SSSource}} is unchanged, and {{NearbySSO}} is its PPDB counterpart.
* *{{NearbyAsteroids}} → {{NearbySSO}}*, now defined:
** the nearest known object predicted within an AP-determined matching radius of each {{DiaSource}}, which may differ between classes of objects, e.g. asteroids and comets;
** its columns: the prediction with its error ellipse, the offset, a rank among nearby DiaSources, and the predicted magnitude, rates and tail directions;
** no link to {{SSObservation}}, because most associated detections were never submitted;
** listing objects predicted in the field but not detected (NULL {{diaSourceId}}) is a possible future extension, not part of this revision.
* *{{SSObservation}} is concrete:*
** one row per Rubin observation accepted by the MPC, keyed by the MPC's {{obsid}};
** it carries the full submitted measurement, from a difference or a science image, with its provenance;
** observations the MPC accepted but hasn't linked to an object are kept.
* *{{ssObjectId}} and {{ssObjectReassocTimeMjdTai}} are to be removed from {{DiaSource}}*, and {{SSSource}}/{{SSObject}} from the APDB.
* *How the record of submitted measurements is kept is now an implementation detail.*

The schema is in [lsst/sdm_schemas#549|https://github.com/lsst/sdm_schemas/pull/549] (DM-55375). The daily build is running at USDF from the current MPC catalog, and is staged for the PPDB loader (DM-55678).

*On the comments so far:*

* *2026-06-25, MPC submissions from DR Solar System processing.* Right: the MPC is not an input to DR Solar System processing. It is an input only to the PPDB Solar System products. {{SSObservation}} already handles observations submitted from different processings, prompt and DRP alike, and records which one each came from.
* *2026-06-30, DiaObject light curves contaminated by SSObjects.* Loading {{NearbySSO}} into Prompt Processing is a natural follow-up. The validation gives what's needed to choose a threshold: an association is real with probability 0.99 at 1″, and 0.2–0.4% of associations are chance coincidences. It also found that Alert Production's own associations, made since 2026-02-18, agree with {{NearbySSO}} 99.8% of the time, but cover only about 54% of the detections {{NearbySSO}} associates within 1″ over the same period. That is one more reason to move this information out of {{DiaSource}}.
* *2026-08-24, what to do with this RFC.* With this revision I think it is ready for review and adoption. On adoption, DM-55375's link can be upgraded to "is triggering", as noted on 2026-07-02.
